            <!-- The spine: **one shape doing two jobs, which is why there is no cross-fade
                 left in this drawing.** Shut, it is the rounded cap joining the two covers down
                 the left-hand side -- the thing whose absence made the old shut pose read as
                 two floating bars. Open, squashed to half its height, it is the dark gutter the
                 flame comes out of, flush with the page tops so it never stands proud of them.
                 The previous rig needed a separate gutter shape fading in over the cream, which
                 is mud; a hinge only needs `scaleY`.

                 Behind both halves, so shut it shows only as the cap past their left edge, and
                 open only as the strip between their inner ends. -->
            <Shape scaleY="0.5" name="spine" id="0:41">
