            <!-- The burst, out and gone. It now belongs to **the burst and not to the whole
                 ignition**: it used to start at 28 and expand across 26 frames, which during
                 the strain was a slow ring leaving a flame that was visibly failing to grow.
                 Two frames after the coil, fast, and fading on `easeOut` so it thins as it
                 goes rather than lingering at full alpha and then vanishing.

                 **Its reach is 1.9 and not 2.6, which is the second time this has been wrong
                 in the same direction.** Scaled up to match a flame three times as tall, the
                 ring threw its dots roughly 230 units clear of a flame 160 wide -- far enough
                 that they stopped reading as sparks coming off it and became pale circles
                 floating in the frame, which at that size look like soap bubbles. Spray has to
                 stay in contact with the thing it sprayed from. -->
            <!-- The burst's spray. **Scale runs 0.85 to 1.35, not 0.2 to 1.14**, and that change
                 is inseparable from moving the node behind the flame. The old range threw the dots
                 outward from a near-point, which is the right gesture for a spray drawn in front
                 and the wrong one for a spray drawn behind: at 0.2 every dot is buried, and
                 opacity peaked while the scale was still 0.41, so the brightest frame was also
                 the most buried one. Starting near 1 puts each dot at the edge of the silhouette
                 as it lights, and the remaining travel carries it clear.

                 Opacity peaks on frame 62 rather than 61 for the same reason: 62 is where the
                 scale crosses 1.0, so the dots are at exactly the positions they were authored
                 at. It is also `linear` now rather than eased into -- a spark lights, it does not
                 swell, which is the same argument as the embers' opacity. -->
