            <!--
              The spray: five embers, each with its own window inside the loop, drifting
              outward as it rises so the group opens into a plume rather than a column.

                e1  0..26   e5  10..64 (the slow one, which travels furthest)
                e2 14..40   e3  28..54   e4  42..68

              Overlapping in pairs, so there is never a frame with nothing in flight and never
              one that looks like a volley. Every window ends at or before 72, which is what
              makes the seam free -- see the note on `embers` in the artboard.

              Opacity is `linear` throughout: an ember is a point of light with no weight, and
              an eased fade on something four pixels across reads as a flicker rather than as
              a curve. Height is eased out, because a spark leaves fast and slows as it cools.
